<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 January, from 98 to 1967.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">International Holocaust Remembrance Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Designated by the United Nations in 2005 to coincide with the liberation of Auschwitz-Birkenau, this day honours the memory of the six million Jewish victims and millions of others murdered by the Nazi regime.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/trajan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trajan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">98 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,928 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trajan becomes Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of Nerva, his adopted son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>, the first emperor born outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, succeeded to the throne. His conquests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> brought the empire to its greatest extent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1302">1302 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">724 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dante Alighieri is sentenced to exile from Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>'s victorious <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-and-white-guelphs">Black Guelphs</a> convicted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> of corruption in his absence. He never returned home, and wrote the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-comedy">Divine Comedy</a>' during his exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1756">1756 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">270 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart is born in Salzburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The son of the court musician Leopold Mozart, he toured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> as a child prodigy. In a life of 35 years he wrote more than 600 works, including 'The Marriage of Figaro' and 'Don Giovanni'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1880">1880 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">146 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Edison patents his incandescent lamp</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edison received US patent 223,898 for a carbon-filament lamp. Others had made electric bulbs, but his long-lasting design and supply system made electric lighting practical.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Siege of Leningrad is lifted after 872 days</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet offensives drove German forces back from Leningrad, ending a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> that began in September 1941. Some 800,000 or more civilians died, most from starvation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet troops liberate Auschwitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> soldiers reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a> and found about 7,000 prisoners left behind. Around 1.1 million people, most of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, were murdered there. The date is now International <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> Remembrance Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire kills three Apollo 1 astronauts during a test</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A flash fire in the pure-oxygen cabin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 1 killed Gus Grissom, Ed White and Roger Chaffee during a launch rehearsal at Cape Kennedy. NASA redesigned the spacecraft before flying again.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Outer Space Treaty signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> signed a treaty barring nuclear weapons from orbit and forbidding any nation from claiming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> or other celestial bodies. It remains the basis of space law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
